== a main that states a projector
  A: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending
  the entry names the server as its projector: true
  A has not projected it: entries 1, the tree head 0
  nor taken it over, long after its settle and quarantine: the tree head 0
  S: 1 entries merged, 0 committed, 0 pending
  S has: the tree head 1

== the main's settings are kept for a start without it (05 2.1)
  A, the main up: [passwords]
  A again, the main down: [passwords]
  B, which never reached the main, the main down: nothing
  A after the main stated nothing, then down: nothing

== a run of pushes projects each entry before the next
  paused at the second push: position 2, 3 pending; entries on the main: 2
  resumed: 0 entries merged, 2 committed, 0 pending
  entries not projected when each was pushed: 0 0 0 0
  entries on the main: 4, the tree head: 4

== the answer to a create is lost; the owner restarts
  A after the failed push: position 0, 1 pending, a push in flight; entries on the main: 1
  restarted, then a write to the same name: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending
  A: f="two"; position 2, 0 pending; entries: 2
  B: f="two"

== a main that does not answer, from the start
  A, the main down: dir/  f="made offline"; position none, 2 pending
  a cycle: failed: no main answered [unreachable]
  A after it: position none, 2 pending
  the main back: 0 pending
  B: dir/  f="made offline"

== an entry whose answer was lost reaches the copies
  A, the next cycle: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 0 pending
  the replica holds the entry: true

== a create that never left; the owner restarts
  A after the failed push: position 0, 1 pending, a push in flight; entries on the main: 0
  restarted: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 0 pending
  A: f="one"; position 1, 0 pending; entries: 1

== an arrival record left by a crash is completed at start
  B after its start, with no cycle: f="again"  g="new"; position 2, 0 pending
  an anchor from before the crash: stale: the frontend lists again
  the next cycle: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 0 pending

== a push refused by a commit that touches nothing pending
  B: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending
  chunks B sent after A's commit got ahead: 0; entries: 2
  B: mine="from B"  theirs="from A"
  A: mine="from B"  theirs="from A"

== more commands than an entry holds
  A: 0 entries merged, 3 committed, 0 pending
  commands per entry: 256, 256, 88; tree head: 3
  B holds 600 links

== a file renamed, then edited, while its upload is held
  A: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 2 pending
  B meanwhile: f="kept"
  once the upload passes, A: position 2, 0 pending
  B: g="EDIT"

== an entry no client can decode, then voided
  A: failed: log entry 2 cannot be followed: fetching and pushing stop until it is voided or this client is upgraded [corrupt/other]
  A: position 1, 1 pending, cannot follow entry 2 (it does not decode: expected a JSON object)
  B: failed: log entry 2 cannot be followed: fetching and pushing stop until it is voided or this client is upgraded [corrupt/other]; position 1, 0 pending, cannot follow entry 2 (it does not decode: expected a JSON object)
  voided. A: 1 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending
  B: 2 entries merged, 0 committed, 0 pending; f="one"  g="behind"
  entries: 3; tree head: 1

== an entry of a later version
  A: failed: log entry 1 cannot be followed: fetching and pushing stop until it is voided or this client is upgraded [corrupt/other]
  A: position 0, 1 pending, cannot follow entry 1 (it is of version 2)
  a void object changes nothing for it: failed: log entry 1 cannot be followed: fetching and pushing stop until it is voided or this client is upgraded [corrupt/other]

== a chunk the main lost before the commit
  A, its create failing: position 0, 1 pending, a push in flight
  A, the chunk gone from the main: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending
  A: position 1, 0 pending
  after the upload ran again: position 1, 0 pending; entries: 1
  B: f="abcdefgh"

== a refused file is committed once written again
  A, renamed, a chunk gone from the main: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 2 pending
  damaged: g
  A, g written again: position 2, 0 pending; damaged: 0
  B: g="ijkl"

== a chunk the main lost, which the cache still holds
  A, renamed, a chunk gone from the main: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending
  damaged: 0; the main holds the chunk again: true

== an edit that inherits a chunk the main lost
  B, an inherited chunk gone from the main: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 1 pending
  damaged: f
  B, a cycle later: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 1 pending

== a parked copy is retried, and the pause flag is where 07 says
  the replica refusing, it holds the chunk: false
  re-armed: true; the replica holds the chunk: true
  paused, the flag exists: true

== an entry its author never projected
  A merges it without waiting for its projection: 1 entries merged, 0 committed, 0 pending
  A: f="one"  g="dead"; tree head: 1 of 2
  an owner whose listener projects, at its first cycle: arrived by state, 0 committed, 0 pending; tree head: 2 of 2
  A commits behind it: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending; tree head: 3 of 3
  a new client arrives by state over the unprojected entries: f="one"  g="dead"  h="after"

== a position that is gone: arrival by state keeps pending work
  B: arrived by state, 1 committed, 0 pending
  B: f="from A"  mine="from B"  shared="from A"  shared (conflicted copy from B)="from B"
  A: f="from A"  mine="from B"  shared="from A"  shared (conflicted copy from B)="from B"

== a file written again with the bytes it had
  A, once the upload ended: position 1, 0 pending

== a write that waits for its base while another file arrives
  B, its write waiting: 1 entries merged, 0 committed, 1 pending
  B, the write made: position 2, 1 pending
  B: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending
  A: f="aZcdefgh"  other="x"

== an uploaded edit whose before-value is lost
  A restarted: position 1, 1 pending
  A: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending
  B: f="WXYZ"

== a write that fails leaves nothing pending
  a write to a folder: refused: dir is a folder
  A: position 1, 0 pending

== the same bytes written on two machines
  B: 1 entries merged, 0 committed, 0 pending; f="abcd"
  B has the file as the main holds it: true
  entries: 1

== a read-only client leaves an entry to those that write
  read-only B: f="abcd"; the tree head 0, takeovers 0
  C, which writes: the tree head 1, takeovers 1

== a poll leaves a change to its batch delay
  A, a second after a poll: position 0, 1 pending
  A, asked to sync: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending

== a configuration the main refuses, then set right
  A: position 0, 1 pending; failing: configured against what the main states [invalid]
  set right: position 1, 0 pending; failing: no

== a paused client leaves another's entry to its projector
  B paused: the tree head 0 of 1, takeovers 0
  B resumed: the tree head 1 of 1, takeovers 1

== two files swapped, over the bytes of one entry
  A: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending
  the swap made 1 entry, over the limit: true
  B: x="bbbb"… y="aaaa"…

== a lazy tree restarted with a create whose answer was lost
  A after the failed push: position none, 1 pending, a push in flight
  restarted and asked nothing: position none, 0 pending

== a file whose mirror entry cannot be decoded, then written
  A writes: done
  A: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 0 pending
  A: f="abcd"  f (conflicted copy from A)="WXYZ"; position 2, 0 pending
  B: f="abcd"  f (conflicted copy from A)="WXYZ"

